        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodfin%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town officially incorporated in 1971, though its roots reach back to the mid‑1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodfin%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Much of Woodfin’s remaining early housing reflects the layout of early 20th‑century mill villages.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodfin%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The French Broad River winds through the town’s western edge, adding a natural waterway to the landscape.",
